('3dfb2abe-0291-5348-a10d-890ebcd5aa1a','c8341a0c-ffa3-5f42-8c95-516bd5a23c81',1,null,null,'spoken & written','money that you are given for doing your job',null,null,'حقوق، دستمزد؛ پرداخت (مالی)؛ حق (سپری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['low Nurses often work long hours for relatively low pay.','good The work was steady and the pay was pretty good.','higher/better Workers demanded higher pay.','equal pay (= the same pay for the same type of work ) The women at the factory went on strike for equal pay.','basic pay British English , base pay American English (= not including overtime pay or bonuses ) The basic pay is so low you end up doing lots of overtime.','take-home pay (= after tax etc has been taken away ) Their average take-home pay is just £120.','overtime pay (= for extra hours that you work ) Their bosses had to approve any overtime pay.','holiday pay British English , vacation pay American English (= pay when you are on holiday ) Servicemen and women get no holiday pay, no overtime, no weekends off.','sick pay (= pay when you are ill ) As a self-employed person, you get no sick pay or benefits.','maternity pay (= pay while a woman takes time off to have a baby ) If you have worked here a year, you are entitled to 3 month’s maternity pay.','redundancy pay British English , severance pay American English (= pay when there is no longer a job for you ) We invested our redundancy pay in a new business venture.','full pay They were immediately suspended on full pay pending a full inquiry.','half pay In 1822 he retired from the army as captain on half pay.','a pay increase Teachers will be awarded a 6% pay increase this year.','a pay rise British English , pay raise American English If you get promoted, will you get a pay rise?','a pay cut Staff were asked to take a 10% pay cut.','a rate of pay ( also a pay rate ) (= the amount paid every hour, week etc ) Many workers in the catering industry are on low rates of pay.','a pay cheque British English , a paycheck American English (= the money you earn every week or month ) Stretching your money until the next pay cheque arrives often becomes difficult.','a pay freeze (= when no one’s pay is increased ) Ministers have approved a public sector pay freeze.','a pay claim British English (= official request for more pay ) The miners voted for strike action in support of their pay claim.','a pay dispute (= disagreement between an employer and employees about pay ) Many flights were cancelled because of a pilots’ pay dispute.','pay and conditions (= the conditions in which people work and the pay they get ) The unions are demanding better pay and conditions.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Staff have been working without pay for the last month.","translation":"کارکنان در ماه گذشته بدون حقوق کار کرده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001180.mp3"},{"sentence":"The tax is deducted from your pay every week.","translation":"مالیات هر هفته از حقوق شما کسر می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001181.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was suspended on full pay until the hearing.","translation":"او با حقوق کامل تا جلسه دادگاه تعلیق شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942371.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
