('6350658b-f33f-5500-a151-6ddfec07f073','013d4a61-a454-5084-a703-ab4d52ce7ff0',1,'move to place','حرکت به مکان','spoken & written','to move something to a particular place or position, especially using your hands','[ always + adverb/preposition ]','see Thesaurus box on 000000','گذاشتن، قرار دادن (در جا)؛ بیان کردن (رک)؛ عقب انداختن (کار)',array['place']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He put the coffee on the table.","translation":"قهوه را روی میز گذاشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282486.mp3"},{"sentence":"Where did you put the programmes?","translation":"برنامه ها رو کجا گذاشتی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282487.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('edf3de3a-7315-5ffc-a694-effb0f29adf4','013d4a61-a454-5084-a703-ab4d52ce7ff0',2,'change somebody’s situation/feelings','تغییر وضعیت/احساسات کسی','spoken & written','to make someone be in a situation or have a feeling','[ always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'وادار کردن کسی در موقعیتی قرار بگیرد یا احساسی داشته باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Don’t put yourself into a situation you can’t handle.","translation":"خود را در موقعیتی قرار ندهید که نتوانید از پس آن برآیید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784854.mp3"},{"sentence":"The long delay had put us all in a bad mood.","translation":"تاخیر طولانی همه ما را در حال بدی قرار داده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282505.mp3"},{"sentence":"I don’t want to put you in danger .","translation":"من نمی خواهم شما را در معرض خطر قرار دهم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784855.mp3"},{"sentence":"Pit closures have put thousands of miners out of a job (= made them lose their job ) .","translation":"بسته شدن گودال هزاران معدنچی را بیکار کرده است (= باعث از دست دادن شغلشان شده است).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282501.mp3"},{"sentence":"His boss resigned and Murphy was put in charge.","translation":"رئیس او استعفا داد و مورفی سرپرستی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784869.mp3"},{"sentence":"Politics puts me to sleep .","translation":"سیاست مرا می خواباند .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784870.mp3"},{"sentence":"A knee injury put him out of action for three months.","translation":"مصدومیت زانو او را به مدت سه ماه از میادین دور کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784876.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('e36b9ec8-1884-5a0f-b7cf-31ecf755407a','013d4a61-a454-5084-a703-ab4d52ce7ff0',3,'write/print something','چیزی بنویس/چاپ','spoken & written','to write or print something or to make a mark with a pen or pencil',null,null,'نوشتن یا چاپ چیزی یا علامت گذاری با قلم یا مداد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Put your name at the top of each answer sheet.","translation":"نام خود را در بالای هر پاسخنامه قرار دهید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282672.mp3"},{"sentence":"He put his signature to the contract (= he signed it to show he agreed with it ) .","translation":"او امضای خود را بر قرارداد (= آن را امضا کرد تا نشان دهد با آن موافق است).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784888.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('72ca8ce8-cec1-5169-bc5e-e041280710e3','013d4a61-a454-5084-a703-ab4d52ce7ff0',4,'express','بیان کنید','spoken & written','to say or write something using words in a particular way','[ always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'گفتن یا نوشتن چیزی با استفاده از کلمات به روشی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['well Sorry, I’m not putting it very well.','simply Put simply, our aim is to create art.','succinctly (= using only a few words ) A Russian economist put it most succinctly: ‘People do not care about carbon.’','mildly (= in a way that is not extreme ) His theory is controversial, to put it mildly.','bluntly/crudely/plainly (= in a direct way that may offend people ) I would put it more bluntly. I think you are wallowing in self-pity.','delicately (= in a way that will not offend people ) He had been drunk, or as Hilton delicately put it, ‘talkative’.','cleverly I didn''t agree with her, but she put her argument so cleverly that I was almost persuaded.','put something another way The dress was too small for me, or, to put it another way, I was too big for it.','put something this/that way Let me put it this way - she''s not as young as she was.','put something like that/this ‘He''s been completely irresponsible.’ ‘I wouldn’t put it quite like that.’','put something into words (= say what you are feeling or thinking ) She couldn’t put her feelings into words.','how shall I/we put it? (= used before saying something in an indirect or polite way ) Mr Lewis is now – how shall we put it? – hardly the influence he once was.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The question was well put.","translation":"سوال به خوبی مطرح شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282518.mp3"},{"sentence":"So it was an accident, an ‘act of God’ if you want to put it like that .","translation":"پس این یک تصادف بود، اگر بخواهید آن را اینطور بیان کنید، یک «عمل خدا» بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784892.mp3"},{"sentence":"When women joined the organization, it ‘took on a new look'', as news reports put it .","translation":"هنگامی که زنان به این سازمان پیوستند، همانطور که گزارش های خبری بیان می کنند، \"ظاهر جدیدی به خود گرفت\".","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000282523.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is hard to put into words (= express ) how I feel now.","translation":"به سختی می توان احساسم را در قالب کلمات بیان کرد (= بیان ).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784901.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s not very musical, to put it mildly (= he’s not musical at all ) .","translation":"او خیلی موزیکال نیست، به زبان ساده (= او اصلا اهل موسیقی نیست).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784905.mp3"},{"sentence":"We get on each other’s nerves, to put it bluntly (= to say exactly what I mean ) .","translation":"اعصاب همدیگر را به صراحت بیان می کنیم (= دقیقاً منظورم را بگویم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784910.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s fairly risky. Or to put it another way (= say it in different words ) , don’t try this at home.","translation":"نسبتاً ریسکی است یا به بیان دیگر (= با کلمات متفاوت بگویید)، این کار را در خانه امتحان نکنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784915.mp3"},{"sentence":"The subject matter makes the painting a little, how shall I put it (= how can I say it politely? ) , undesirable for public display.","translation":"موضوع باعث می شود نقاشی کمی، چگونه آن را (= چگونه می توانم آن را مودبانه بگویم؟) نامطلوب برای نمایش عمومی.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001784920.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
