('eec45b12-f4c5-5d17-8cfc-2c583fe4eb8b','a010d5e7-fdfb-511a-8c77-27759e793ca7',9,'chemical','شیمیایی','technical','a chemical substance that combines with an acid to form a salt','[ countable ]',null,'یک ماده شیمیایی که با اسید ترکیب می شود و نمک می سازد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b96b1fd3-a0af-559a-93f9-6774294e7822','a010d5e7-fdfb-511a-8c77-27759e793ca7',10,'numbers','اعداد','technical','the number in relation to which a number system or mathematical table is built up, for example 10 in the decimal system','[ countable usually singular ]',null,'عددی که در رابطه با آن یک سیستم اعداد یا جدول ریاضی ساخته شده است، به عنوان مثال 10 در سیستم اعشاری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('cc11a2b5-8f02-5d90-81e4-b79398b4eb9e','a010d5e7-fdfb-511a-8c77-27759e793ca7',11,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'touch base (with somebody)','قاعده، پایه؛ مبنا؛ مقر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1458e3aa-4769-5672-80c3-8d87db47ddce','e1684e81-7c65-5088-8f8c-e55d9f929f05',1,null,null,'spoken & written','not having good moral principles',null,null,'نداشتن اصول اخلاقی خوب','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"base attitudes and desires","translation":"نگرش ها و خواسته های پایه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000936200.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c84f3ca6-059d-546d-a9b9-653d16e1620e','c4edeffd-012e-5b51-b995-08f6a6be7d32',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if you take a bath, you wash your body in a bath',null,null,'لگن، وان (حمام)؛ حمام‌کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a bath especially British English , take a bath especially American English She usually has a bath in the evening.','give somebody a bath He''s upstairs giving the baby a bath.','get in/into/out of the bath I had to get out of the bath to answer the phone.','a quick bath It''s easier to take a shower than a quick bath.','a long bath A long hot bath is a great way of relaxing.','a hot/warm/cool bath Why don''t you have a nice warm bath?','a bubble bath (= with nice-smelling bubbles in it ) She likes to destress by taking a bubble bath.','bath time (= the time when someone, usually a child, has a bath ) Come on, Lucy, it''s bath time.','bath taps British English The water coming out of the bath taps was freezing cold.','a bath towel She handed him a soft white bath towel.','a bath mat (= small rug on the floor by the bath ) The bath mat was soaking wet.','bath water The bath water is getting cold.','bath salts/crystals (= a substance that you put in a bath to make it smell nice ) She bought me some lavender bath salts.','bath toy (= for a child to play with in the bath ) Bath toys are great for babies who''ve just learned to sit.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"After a week of camping, I really needed a bath.","translation":"بعد از یک هفته کمپینگ، واقعاً به حمام نیاز داشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001003796.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll have a bath and go to bed.","translation":"حمام می‌کنم و می‌خوابم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001658828.mp3"},{"sentence":"How often do you take a bath?","translation":"چند وقت یکبار حمام می کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001989789.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll give the children their bath (= wash them in a bath ) .","translation":"من بچه ها را غسل خواهم داد (= آنها را در غسل بشویم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001658829.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('fd42c10a-67bf-5d01-bc4c-d1c86ea5fde0','c4edeffd-012e-5b51-b995-08f6a6be7d32',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a large long container that you fill with water and sit or lie in to wash yourself',null,null,'ظرف دراز بزرگی که پر از آب می‌کنید و می‌نشینید یا دراز می‌کشید تا خود را بشویید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a bath especially British English , take a bath especially American English She usually has a bath in the evening.','give somebody a bath He''s upstairs giving the baby a bath.','get in/into/out of the bath I had to get out of the bath to answer the phone.','a quick bath It''s easier to take a shower than a quick bath.','a long bath A long hot bath is a great way of relaxing.','a hot/warm/cool bath Why don''t you have a nice warm bath?','a bubble bath (= with nice-smelling bubbles in it ) She likes to destress by taking a bubble bath.','bath time (= the time when someone, usually a child, has a bath ) Come on, Lucy, it''s bath time.','bath taps British English The water coming out of the bath taps was freezing cold.','a bath towel She handed him a soft white bath towel.','a bath mat (= small rug on the floor by the bath ) The bath mat was soaking wet.','bath water The bath water is getting cold.','bath salts/crystals (= a substance that you put in a bath to make it smell nice ) She bought me some lavender bath salts.','bath toy (= for a child to play with in the bath ) Bath toys are great for babies who''ve just learned to sit.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
