('b74c5008-a2d6-5234-8c68-dbeeaf2a45db','1ca7a99c-53f7-5426-a07c-3926e0a954b3',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'on your bike!','دوچرخه (کوتاه‌شده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go somewhere by bike I usually go to work by bike.','ride a bike Her Dad taught her to ride a bike and to drive.','get on/off a bike He got off his bike and walked with her for a while.','rent a bike ( also hire a bike British English ) You can rent bikes and explore the island’s cycle paths.','a mountain bike (= a strong bicycle for riding over rough ground ) They went out for a country ride on their mountain bikes.','a racing bike He bought a cool new racing bike.','an exercise bike (= used for exercising indoors ) I usually go on the exercise bike and the rowing machine.','a bike ride We used to go for long bike rides in the summer holidays.','a bike race The Tour de France is a famous bike race.','a bike shed They used to meet behind the bike sheds at school.','a bike rack (= a metal frame that you can attach your bike to ) All stations should provide bike racks for passengers.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('12018414-045c-5111-8087-7dab396e640f','60ce9f73-62ca-5a39-a746-c1282a3ec4f3',1,null,null,'informal','to ride a bicycle','[ intransitive always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'برای دوچرخه سواری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She bikes to work every day.","translation":"او هر روز با دوچرخه به محل کار می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001017725.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7ea06434-273a-5af7-be15-5721af868c2a','60ce9f73-62ca-5a39-a746-c1282a3ec4f3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to take something to someone by motorcycle in order to get it there quickly','[ transitive ]',null,'بردن چیزی با موتورسیکلت برای کسی تا سریع به آنجا برسند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’re late for our deadline. Can you bike the photos over to us?","translation":"ما به مهلت خود دیر رسیدیم. آیا می توانید عکس ها را برای ما دوچرخه سواری کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001806023.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8c830bb4-d12f-5124-8d56-d782dbcab041','7db883df-efdb-58fe-af0f-d400a2168694',1,'request for payment','درخواست پرداخت','spoken & written','a written list showing how much you have to pay for services you have received , work that has been done etc',null,null,'صورت‌حساب، قبض؛ لایحه، طرح قانون','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay a bill Most people pay their bills on time.','settle a bill (= pay it ) She went down to the lobby to settle the bill for their rooms.','foot the bill/pick up the bill (= pay for something, especially when you do not want to ) Taxpayers will probably have to foot the bill.','run up a bill (= use a lot of something so that you have a big bill to pay ) It’s easy to run up a big bill on your mobile phone.','face a bill (= have a lot to pay on a bill ) They were facing a mounting legal bill.','cut/reduce a bill We need to find a way to cut our fuel bill.','a bill comes to something (= is for that amount ) The bill came to $60.','a big/huge bill Turn off the lights or we’ll get a huge electricity bill.','an electricity/gas/phone etc bill I’ll have to pay the gas bill too next month.','a hotel bill He paid the hotel bill by credit card.','a tax bill There are various ways you can reduce your tax bill.','an unpaid bill She had unpaid bills amounting to £3,000.','an outstanding bill (= still unpaid ) He still didn’t have enough to pay his outstanding bills.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The bill for the repairs came to $650.","translation":"صورتحساب تعمیرات به 650 دلار رسید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001017825.mp3"},{"sentence":"Have you paid the phone bill?","translation":"آیا قبض تلفن را پرداخت کرده اید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001017828.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4bcfef8d-a14c-5710-ad2d-75e4dc7df21e','7db883df-efdb-58fe-af0f-d400a2168694',2,'restaurant','رستوران','spoken & written','a list showing how much you have to pay for food you have eaten in a restaurant',null,null,'لیستی که نشان می دهد چقدر باید برای غذایی که در یک رستوران خورده اید بپردازید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay a bill Most people pay their bills on time.','settle a bill (= pay it ) She went down to the lobby to settle the bill for their rooms.','foot the bill/pick up the bill (= pay for something, especially when you do not want to ) Taxpayers will probably have to foot the bill.','run up a bill (= use a lot of something so that you have a big bill to pay ) It’s easy to run up a big bill on your mobile phone.','face a bill (= have a lot to pay on a bill ) They were facing a mounting legal bill.','cut/reduce a bill We need to find a way to cut our fuel bill.','a bill comes to something (= is for that amount ) The bill came to $60.','a big/huge bill Turn off the lights or we’ll get a huge electricity bill.','an electricity/gas/phone etc bill I’ll have to pay the gas bill too next month.','a hotel bill He paid the hotel bill by credit card.','a tax bill There are various ways you can reduce your tax bill.','an unpaid bill She had unpaid bills amounting to £3,000.','an outstanding bill (= still unpaid ) He still didn’t have enough to pay his outstanding bills.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Could we have the bill, please?","translation":"آیا می توانیم صورتحساب را داشته باشیم، لطفا؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001017840.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('493bff30-c0f9-5579-8bec-94155b1497fb','7db883df-efdb-58fe-af0f-d400a2168694',3,'law','قانون','spoken & written','a written proposal for a new law , that is brought to a parliament so that it can be discussed',null,null,'یک پیشنهاد مکتوب برای قانون جدید، که به مجلس ارائه می شود تا در مورد آن بحث شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay a bill Most people pay their bills on time.','settle a bill (= pay it ) She went down to the lobby to settle the bill for their rooms.','foot the bill/pick up the bill (= pay for something, especially when you do not want to ) Taxpayers will probably have to foot the bill.','run up a bill (= use a lot of something so that you have a big bill to pay ) It’s easy to run up a big bill on your mobile phone.','face a bill (= have a lot to pay on a bill ) They were facing a mounting legal bill.','cut/reduce a bill We need to find a way to cut our fuel bill.','a bill comes to something (= is for that amount ) The bill came to $60.','a big/huge bill Turn off the lights or we’ll get a huge electricity bill.','an electricity/gas/phone etc bill I’ll have to pay the gas bill too next month.','a hotel bill He paid the hotel bill by credit card.','a tax bill There are various ways you can reduce your tax bill.','an unpaid bill She had unpaid bills amounting to £3,000.','an outstanding bill (= still unpaid ) He still didn’t have enough to pay his outstanding bills.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The House of Representatives passed a new gun-control bill.","translation":"مجلس نمایندگان لایحه جدید کنترل سلاح را تصویب کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001017849.mp3"},{"sentence":"The senator introduced a bill that would increase the minimum wage.","translation":"این سناتور لایحه ای را ارائه کرد که حداقل دستمزد را افزایش می داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001732421.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
