('b15325e7-7ad4-5a31-8048-35d841bd8946','05320224-fcb5-51f9-91c8-4feeb87fce83',1,'BAD EFFECT','اثر بد','spoken & written','an action or event that causes difficulty or sadness for someone',null,null,'ضربه، مصیبت؛ کوتاهی بزرگ (در کاری)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a big/major/serious/heavy blow The earthquake was a serious blow to the area’s tourism industry.','a severe/terrible/awful blow The news was a terrible blow for his family.','a bitter blow (= extremely disappointing ) Their defeat was a bitter blow.','a cruel/devastating/crushing blow (= extremely hard to bear ) Her loss came as a devastating blow to her father.','a body blow (= a very serious difficulty which could cause something to fail completely ) A tax on books would be a body blow for education.','a mortal/fatal/death blow (= causing something to end ) When he quit it dealt a mortal blow to the show.','be a blow I can’t deny his leaving was a blow.','deal a blow to somebody/something The 1982 drought dealt a devastating blow to the country.','come as a blow to somebody His sudden death came as a huge blow to us all.','deliver a blow Opinion polls delivered a nasty blow to the Tory leader.','suffer/receive a blow Our team suffered a blow when Paul was sent off the field.','soften/cushion the blow (= make it easier to deal with ) There are various ways to soften the blow of redundancy among staff.','be a bit of a blow British English especially spoken (= be disappointing or cause problems for you ) The result was a bit of a blow for the team.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Joe resigned, which was a severe blow because we needed him desperately.","translation":"جو استعفا داد که ضربه سختی بود زیرا ما به شدت به او نیاز داشتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001892276.mp3"},{"sentence":"His mother’s death was a shattering blow .","translation":"مرگ مادرش ضربه مهلکی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001769610.mp3"},{"sentence":"The election result dealt a further blow to the party.","translation":"نتیجه انتخابات ضربه بیشتری به حزب وارد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001892284.mp3"},{"sentence":"The factory closures came as a blow to the local economy.","translation":"تعطیلی کارخانه ضربه ای به اقتصاد محلی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001892290.mp3"},{"sentence":"The final blow for many firms was the government’s abolition of import duties.","translation":"آخرین ضربه برای بسیاری از شرکت ها لغو تعرفه واردات از سوی دولت بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001892298.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('2c38c7f9-9d4b-5f06-bf90-5481b59f09d2','05320224-fcb5-51f9-91c8-4feeb87fce83',2,'hard hit','ضربه سخت','spoken & written','a hard hit with someone’s hand, a tool , or a weapon',null,null,'ضربه محکم با دست، ابزار یا سلاح کسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a big/major/serious/heavy blow The earthquake was a serious blow to the area’s tourism industry.','a severe/terrible/awful blow The news was a terrible blow for his family.','a bitter blow (= extremely disappointing ) Their defeat was a bitter blow.','a cruel/devastating/crushing blow (= extremely hard to bear ) Her loss came as a devastating blow to her father.','a body blow (= a very serious difficulty which could cause something to fail completely ) A tax on books would be a body blow for education.','a mortal/fatal/death blow (= causing something to end ) When he quit it dealt a mortal blow to the show.','be a blow I can’t deny his leaving was a blow.','deal a blow to somebody/something The 1982 drought dealt a devastating blow to the country.','come as a blow to somebody His sudden death came as a huge blow to us all.','deliver a blow Opinion polls delivered a nasty blow to the Tory leader.','suffer/receive a blow Our team suffered a blow when Paul was sent off the field.','soften/cushion the blow (= make it easier to deal with ) There are various ways to soften the blow of redundancy among staff.','be a bit of a blow British English especially spoken (= be disappointing or cause problems for you ) The result was a bit of a blow for the team.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She died from a heavy blow to the head.","translation":"او بر اثر ضربه شدیدی که به سرش وارد شد جان باخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001025255.mp3"},{"sentence":"He struck a blow which threw her to the floor.","translation":"او ضربه ای زد که او را روی زمین انداخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001677206.mp3"},{"sentence":"Martin received a blow on the nose.","translation":"مارتین ضربه ای به بینی خورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001677210.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had been struck a glancing blow (= a blow that did not hit him directly ) by the car.","translation":"ضربه ای که مستقیماً به او اصابت نکرده بود توسط ماشین به او زده شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001025256.mp3"},{"sentence":"He gave her a violent blow to the head.","translation":"ضربه شدیدی به سرش زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001783092.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
