('2df8bcd4-0468-54d4-8fc4-fb83fd2f79f6','799e3383-848b-57f9-b628-d9f3769f6281',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make arrangements to stay in a place, eat in a restaurant, go to a theatre etc at a particular time in the future','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'رزرو کردن (اتاق، میز، بلیت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['book a holiday People often book their holidays in January.','book a trip I booked the whole trip on the Internet.','book a flight He picked up the phone and booked a flight to Barcelona.','book a ticket It’s cheaper if you book your train ticket in advance.','book a table (= in a restaurant ) I’ll book a table for 7.30 tomorrow evening.','book a room/hotel Ross found a good hotel and booked a room.','book a seat She booked me a seat on the 9 am flight.','book a place on something Students are advised to book a place on the course early.','book early We recommend you book early to avoid disappointment.','book (well) in advance There are only 20 places, so it is essential to book well in advance.','book online (= on the Internet ) It’s much easier to book tickets online.','be fully booked (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold ) I’m afraid that show is fully booked.','be booked solid (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold for a long period ) The restaurant’s booked solid for the whole of the Christmas period.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Have you booked a holiday this year?","translation":"آیا برای تعطیلات امسال رزرو کرده اید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649709.mp3"},{"sentence":"The flight was already fully booked (= no more seats were available ) .","translation":"پرواز قبلاً به طور کامل رزرو شده بود (= هیچ صندلی دیگری در دسترس نبود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001027973.mp3"},{"sentence":"To get tickets, you have to book in advance .","translation":"برای تهیه بلیط باید از قبل رزرو کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649714.mp3"},{"sentence":"The show’s booked solid (= all the tickets have been sold ) until February.","translation":"نمایش کاملاً رزرو شده است (= همه بلیت ها فروخته شده است) تا فوریه.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001027977.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('31c36955-f0cb-52bc-a828-64692ff1d4d2','799e3383-848b-57f9-b628-d9f3769f6281',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to arrange for someone such as a singer to perform on a particular date','[ transitive ]',null,'ترتیب دادن برای اجرای شخصی مانند خواننده در یک تاریخ خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['book a holiday People often book their holidays in January.','book a trip I booked the whole trip on the Internet.','book a flight He picked up the phone and booked a flight to Barcelona.','book a ticket It’s cheaper if you book your train ticket in advance.','book a table (= in a restaurant ) I’ll book a table for 7.30 tomorrow evening.','book a room/hotel Ross found a good hotel and booked a room.','book a seat She booked me a seat on the 9 am flight.','book a place on something Students are advised to book a place on the course early.','book early We recommend you book early to avoid disappointment.','book (well) in advance There are only 20 places, so it is essential to book well in advance.','book online (= on the Internet ) It’s much easier to book tickets online.','be fully booked (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold ) I’m afraid that show is fully booked.','be booked solid (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold for a long period ) The restaurant’s booked solid for the whole of the Christmas period.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The band was booked for a benefit show in Los Angeles.","translation":"گروه برای یک نمایش سودمند در لس آنجلس رزرو شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649722.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b356218d-bd42-5e22-91a3-e758f7044f44','799e3383-848b-57f9-b628-d9f3769f6281',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be booked up','رزرو کردن (اتاق، میز، بلیت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['book a holiday People often book their holidays in January.','book a trip I booked the whole trip on the Internet.','book a flight He picked up the phone and booked a flight to Barcelona.','book a ticket It’s cheaper if you book your train ticket in advance.','book a table (= in a restaurant ) I’ll book a table for 7.30 tomorrow evening.','book a room/hotel Ross found a good hotel and booked a room.','book a seat She booked me a seat on the 9 am flight.','book a place on something Students are advised to book a place on the course early.','book early We recommend you book early to avoid disappointment.','book (well) in advance There are only 20 places, so it is essential to book well in advance.','book online (= on the Internet ) It’s much easier to book tickets online.','be fully booked (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold ) I’m afraid that show is fully booked.','be booked solid (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold for a long period ) The restaurant’s booked solid for the whole of the Christmas period.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('a1bc946f-8c14-5581-8e63-9a0dfc3b633f','799e3383-848b-57f9-b628-d9f3769f6281',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to arrange for someone to go to a hotel , fly on a plane etc','[ transitive ]',null,'ترتیب دادن برای کسی که به هتل برود، با هواپیما پرواز کند و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['book a holiday People often book their holidays in January.','book a trip I booked the whole trip on the Internet.','book a flight He picked up the phone and booked a flight to Barcelona.','book a ticket It’s cheaper if you book your train ticket in advance.','book a table (= in a restaurant ) I’ll book a table for 7.30 tomorrow evening.','book a room/hotel Ross found a good hotel and booked a room.','book a seat She booked me a seat on the 9 am flight.','book a place on something Students are advised to book a place on the course early.','book early We recommend you book early to avoid disappointment.','book (well) in advance There are only 20 places, so it is essential to book well in advance.','book online (= on the Internet ) It’s much easier to book tickets online.','be fully booked (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold ) I’m afraid that show is fully booked.','be booked solid (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold for a long period ) The restaurant’s booked solid for the whole of the Christmas period.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ve booked you a flight on Saturday.","translation":"من برای شما یک پرواز در روز شنبه رزرو کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649735.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll book you in at the Hilton.","translation":"من شما را در هیلتون رزرو می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649738.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('742a5be5-38f8-5653-8925-b3aa8249d1aa','799e3383-848b-57f9-b628-d9f3769f6281',5,null,null,'spoken & written','to put someone’s name officially in police records , along with the charge made against them','[ transitive ]',null,'برای درج نام شخصی به طور رسمی در سوابق پلیس، همراه با اتهامی که علیه آنها مطرح شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['book a holiday People often book their holidays in January.','book a trip I booked the whole trip on the Internet.','book a flight He picked up the phone and booked a flight to Barcelona.','book a ticket It’s cheaper if you book your train ticket in advance.','book a table (= in a restaurant ) I’ll book a table for 7.30 tomorrow evening.','book a room/hotel Ross found a good hotel and booked a room.','book a seat She booked me a seat on the 9 am flight.','book a place on something Students are advised to book a place on the course early.','book early We recommend you book early to avoid disappointment.','book (well) in advance There are only 20 places, so it is essential to book well in advance.','book online (= on the Internet ) It’s much easier to book tickets online.','be fully booked (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold ) I’m afraid that show is fully booked.','be booked solid (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold for a long period ) The restaurant’s booked solid for the whole of the Christmas period.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Smith was booked on suspicion of attempted murder.","translation":"اسمیت به ظن تلاش برای قتل محکوم شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001027991.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('71c83557-f885-5a2f-a176-79b43d5149a4','799e3383-848b-57f9-b628-d9f3769f6281',6,null,null,'spoken & written','when a referee in a sports game books a player who has broken the rules , he or she officially writes down the player’s name in a book as a punishment','[ transitive ]',null,'وقتی یک داور در یک بازی ورزشی به بازیکنی که قوانین را زیر پا گذاشته است، کارت داوری می‌گیرد، به عنوان تنبیه، رسماً نام بازیکن را در کتابی می‌نویسد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['book a holiday People often book their holidays in January.','book a trip I booked the whole trip on the Internet.','book a flight He picked up the phone and booked a flight to Barcelona.','book a ticket It’s cheaper if you book your train ticket in advance.','book a table (= in a restaurant ) I’ll book a table for 7.30 tomorrow evening.','book a room/hotel Ross found a good hotel and booked a room.','book a seat She booked me a seat on the 9 am flight.','book a place on something Students are advised to book a place on the course early.','book early We recommend you book early to avoid disappointment.','book (well) in advance There are only 20 places, so it is essential to book well in advance.','book online (= on the Internet ) It’s much easier to book tickets online.','be fully booked (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold ) I’m afraid that show is fully booked.','be booked solid (= all the seats, tickets etc are sold for a long period ) The restaurant’s booked solid for the whole of the Christmas period.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('44c1fd6f-4b81-5181-9119-600cd4a0a3b8','7f3f3ff9-7f65-5d1d-bb7a-5f805117aef5',1,'increase in business','افزایش در کسب و کار','spoken & written','a quick increase of business activity','[ singular ]','boom town','رکود… نه؛ اوج‌گیری، رونق اقتصادی؛ بوم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic boom the post-war economic boom','a property/housing boom (= a sudden increase in house prices ) People made a lot of money in the 1980s property boom.','a consumer/spending boom (= a sudden increase in the amount people spend ) Various factors caused the consumer boom.','a building/construction boom (= a sudden increase in building work ) There’s been a recent construction boom in the Gulf.','an investment boom the investment boom of the past few years','cause/lead to a boom Tax cuts sometimes lead to an economic boom.','trigger/spark a boom (= start it ) The lower interest rates triggered an economic boom.','fuel a boom (= add to it ) The energy crisis is fuelling a boom in alternative energy.','enjoy a boom Since then, China has enjoyed a remarkable boom.','the boom years/times the boom years of the late 1980s','go from boom to bust (= change from doing very well economically to doing very badly ) The Mexican economy went from boom to bust very quickly.','at the height of the boom They sold their house at the height of the boom.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The boom has created job opportunities.","translation":"رونق فرصت های شغلی ایجاد کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649161.mp3"},{"sentence":"a sudden boom in the housing market","translation":"رونق ناگهانی در بازار مسکن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001028592.mp3"},{"sentence":"the post-war property boom","translation":"رونق املاک پس از جنگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001028595.mp3"},{"sentence":"In boom times, airlines do well.","translation":"در دوران رونق، خطوط هوایی خوب عمل می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001028598.mp3"},{"sentence":"the economic boom of the 1950s","translation":"رونق اقتصادی دهه 1950","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649162.mp3"},{"sentence":"The economy went from boom to bust (= from increasing to decreasing ) very quickly.","translation":"اقتصاد خیلی سریع از رونق به رکود (= از افزایش به کاهش) رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649166.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('0a2afd0d-fe31-5ad7-8b8d-068dd958e15e','7f3f3ff9-7f65-5d1d-bb7a-5f805117aef5',2,'when something is popular','وقتی چیزی محبوب است','spoken & written','an increase in how popular or successful something is, or in how often it happens','[ singular ]','baby boom','افزایش در میزان محبوبیت یا موفقیت یک چیزی یا تعداد دفعات وقوع آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an economic boom the post-war economic boom','a property/housing boom (= a sudden increase in house prices ) People made a lot of money in the 1980s property boom.','a consumer/spending boom (= a sudden increase in the amount people spend ) Various factors caused the consumer boom.','a building/construction boom (= a sudden increase in building work ) There’s been a recent construction boom in the Gulf.','an investment boom the investment boom of the past few years','cause/lead to a boom Tax cuts sometimes lead to an economic boom.','trigger/spark a boom (= start it ) The lower interest rates triggered an economic boom.','fuel a boom (= add to it ) The energy crisis is fuelling a boom in alternative energy.','enjoy a boom Since then, China has enjoyed a remarkable boom.','the boom years/times the boom years of the late 1980s','go from boom to bust (= change from doing very well economically to doing very badly ) The Mexican economy went from boom to bust very quickly.','at the height of the boom They sold their house at the height of the boom.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the disco boom of the 1970s","translation":"رونق دیسکو در دهه 1970","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649172.mp3"},{"sentence":"the boom in youth soccer in the U.S.","translation":"رونق فوتبال جوانان در ایالات متحده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001649175.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
