('647cd5ef-8edb-51b8-8740-713397571a6d','23d7cfea-495e-5596-8adb-c38c342cb2ad',1,null,null,'spoken & written','plants such as wheat , barley , and oats or their seeds','[ uncountable ]',null,'غلات (گندم، جو)؛ ذرت (آمریکایی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"fields of corn","translation":"مزارع ذرت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001711438.mp3"},{"sentence":"an ear of corn (= the top part of this plant where the seeds grow )","translation":"یک خوشه (= قسمت بالای این گیاه که دانه ها در آن رشد می کنند)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001176355.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('eb6237ac-167b-56c5-a20b-04197113244e','23d7cfea-495e-5596-8adb-c38c342cb2ad',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a tall plant with large yellow seeds that grow together on a cob (= long hard part ) , which is cooked and eaten as a vegetable or fed to animals','[ uncountable ]','corn on the cob','گیاهی بلند با دانه های زرد درشت که با هم روی بلال می رویند (= قسمت سخت بلند) که پخته و به عنوان سبزی خورده می شود یا به حیوانات می خورند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"All our chickens are fed on corn.","translation":"همه جوجه های ما از ذرت تغذیه می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001711451.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('bcd81f0a-25c9-5240-978c-c283cea96860','23d7cfea-495e-5596-8adb-c38c342cb2ad',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a painful area of thick hard skin on your foot','[ countable ]',null,'یک ناحیه دردناک از پوست سخت ضخیم روی پای شما','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('383abcb5-98b9-5d47-a511-62b379c0d0f7','6ad205cd-0b65-56e7-8f17-832062b9af92',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the amount of money that you have to pay in order to buy, do, or produce something','[ countable ]','cost of living','بها، هزینه؛ (اسراف) زیان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay the cost of something I’m not sure how I’m going to pay the cost of going to college.','cover the cost (= pay for something ) The money he had saved just covered the cost of the trip.','meet/bear the cost of something (= pay for something, especially with difficulty ) His family were unable to meet the cost of his operation.','afford the cost of something We can’t afford the cost of a holiday abroad this year.','reduce/lower/bring down the cost If you go later in the year, it will bring down the cost of your holiday.','cut the cost (= reduce it ) The government has promised to cut the cost of medical care.','increase/push up the cost The new tax will increase the cost of owning a car.','the cost rises/goes up The cost of electricity has risen again.','the cost falls/goes down Airline costs have fallen considerably.','high/low the high cost of fuel','the average cost What’s the average cost of a wedding in the UK?','an extra/additional cost At the campsite, many activities are available at no extra cost.','the full/total cost Experts are still assessing the full cost of the disaster.','the estimated cost (= one that is guessed and may not be exact ) The estimated cost was in the region of £3,000.','the annual/monthly cost This figure represents the annual cost of a loan.','labour/production/transport etc costs They had to pay £30,000 in legal costs.','running/operating costs (= the amount it costs to run a business, a machine etc ) The new technology is cheaper and the running costs are lower.','borrowing costs (= the amount it costs to borrow money from a bank ) Interest rates and borrowing costs are likely to be higher next year.','the cost of living (= the amount you need to pay for food, clothes etc ) People are complaining about the rising cost of living.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the cost of accommodation","translation":"هزینه اقامت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683881.mp3"},{"sentence":"I offered to pay the cost of the taxi.","translation":"من پیشنهاد دادم هزینه تاکسی را بپردازم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683880.mp3"},{"sentence":"Insurance to cover the cost of a funeral is possible.","translation":"بیمه برای پوشش هزینه مراسم ختم امکان پذیر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845529.mp3"},{"sentence":"This doesn’t include the cost of repairing the damage.","translation":"این شامل هزینه تعمیر آسیب نمی شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683884.mp3"},{"sentence":"The new building’s going up at a cost of $82 million.","translation":"ساختمان جدید با هزینه 82 میلیون دلار در حال ساخت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001111898.mp3"},{"sentence":"low cost housing","translation":"مسکن کم هزینه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683887.mp3"},{"sentence":"the high cost of production","translation":"هزینه بالای تولید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001111901.mp3"},{"sentence":"Travel insurance is included at no extra cost .","translation":"بیمه مسافرتی بدون هزینه اضافی شامل می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00192.mp3"},{"sentence":"The funds will just cover the museum’s running costs .","translation":"این بودجه فقط هزینه های جاری موزه را پوشش می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001939929.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('48335500-1a68-5e51-bbfa-c94b32c58686','6ad205cd-0b65-56e7-8f17-832062b9af92',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'costs','بها، هزینه؛ (اسراف) زیان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay the cost of something I’m not sure how I’m going to pay the cost of going to college.','cover the cost (= pay for something ) The money he had saved just covered the cost of the trip.','meet/bear the cost of something (= pay for something, especially with difficulty ) His family were unable to meet the cost of his operation.','afford the cost of something We can’t afford the cost of a holiday abroad this year.','reduce/lower/bring down the cost If you go later in the year, it will bring down the cost of your holiday.','cut the cost (= reduce it ) The government has promised to cut the cost of medical care.','increase/push up the cost The new tax will increase the cost of owning a car.','the cost rises/goes up The cost of electricity has risen again.','the cost falls/goes down Airline costs have fallen considerably.','high/low the high cost of fuel','the average cost What’s the average cost of a wedding in the UK?','an extra/additional cost At the campsite, many activities are available at no extra cost.','the full/total cost Experts are still assessing the full cost of the disaster.','the estimated cost (= one that is guessed and may not be exact ) The estimated cost was in the region of £3,000.','the annual/monthly cost This figure represents the annual cost of a loan.','labour/production/transport etc costs They had to pay £30,000 in legal costs.','running/operating costs (= the amount it costs to run a business, a machine etc ) The new technology is cheaper and the running costs are lower.','borrowing costs (= the amount it costs to borrow money from a bank ) Interest rates and borrowing costs are likely to be higher next year.','the cost of living (= the amount you need to pay for food, clothes etc ) People are complaining about the rising cost of living.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c999ec63-dfc8-584c-bfde-728241ccb99d','6ad205cd-0b65-56e7-8f17-832062b9af92',3,null,null,'spoken & written','something that you lose, give away, damage etc in order to achieve something','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'چیزی که برای رسیدن به چیزی از دست می دهید، می بخشید، آسیب می بینید و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay the cost of something I’m not sure how I’m going to pay the cost of going to college.','cover the cost (= pay for something ) The money he had saved just covered the cost of the trip.','meet/bear the cost of something (= pay for something, especially with difficulty ) His family were unable to meet the cost of his operation.','afford the cost of something We can’t afford the cost of a holiday abroad this year.','reduce/lower/bring down the cost If you go later in the year, it will bring down the cost of your holiday.','cut the cost (= reduce it ) The government has promised to cut the cost of medical care.','increase/push up the cost The new tax will increase the cost of owning a car.','the cost rises/goes up The cost of electricity has risen again.','the cost falls/goes down Airline costs have fallen considerably.','high/low the high cost of fuel','the average cost What’s the average cost of a wedding in the UK?','an extra/additional cost At the campsite, many activities are available at no extra cost.','the full/total cost Experts are still assessing the full cost of the disaster.','the estimated cost (= one that is guessed and may not be exact ) The estimated cost was in the region of £3,000.','the annual/monthly cost This figure represents the annual cost of a loan.','labour/production/transport etc costs They had to pay £30,000 in legal costs.','running/operating costs (= the amount it costs to run a business, a machine etc ) The new technology is cheaper and the running costs are lower.','borrowing costs (= the amount it costs to borrow money from a bank ) Interest rates and borrowing costs are likely to be higher next year.','the cost of living (= the amount you need to pay for food, clothes etc ) People are complaining about the rising cost of living.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She had kept her promise to Christine, but at what cost to herself?","translation":"او به قول خود به کریستین عمل کرده بود، اما به چه قیمتی برای خودش؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683907.mp3"},{"sentence":"They need to weigh up the costs and benefits (= disadvantages and advantages ) of regulation.","translation":"آنها باید هزینه ها و منافع (= معایب و مزایا) مقررات را بسنجید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683911.mp3"},{"sentence":"He’s determined to win, whatever the cost (= no matter how much work, money, risk etc is needed ) .","translation":"او مصمم است که برنده شود، به هر قیمتی که باشد (= مهم نیست که چقدر کار، پول، ریسک و غیره مورد نیاز است).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001111924.mp3"},{"sentence":"We must avoid a scandal at all costs (= whatever happens ) .","translation":"ما باید به هر قیمتی از رسوایی جلوگیری کنیم (= هر اتفاقی که بیفتد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001111928.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('2e8e96ff-079c-5424-a9a6-5a93bd8cc014','6ad205cd-0b65-56e7-8f17-832062b9af92',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the price that someone pays for something that they are going to sell','[ singular ]',null,'قیمتی که کسی برای چیزی که قرار است بفروشد می پردازد',array['cost price']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['pay the cost of something I’m not sure how I’m going to pay the cost of going to college.','cover the cost (= pay for something ) The money he had saved just covered the cost of the trip.','meet/bear the cost of something (= pay for something, especially with difficulty ) His family were unable to meet the cost of his operation.','afford the cost of something We can’t afford the cost of a holiday abroad this year.','reduce/lower/bring down the cost If you go later in the year, it will bring down the cost of your holiday.','cut the cost (= reduce it ) The government has promised to cut the cost of medical care.','increase/push up the cost The new tax will increase the cost of owning a car.','the cost rises/goes up The cost of electricity has risen again.','the cost falls/goes down Airline costs have fallen considerably.','high/low the high cost of fuel','the average cost What’s the average cost of a wedding in the UK?','an extra/additional cost At the campsite, many activities are available at no extra cost.','the full/total cost Experts are still assessing the full cost of the disaster.','the estimated cost (= one that is guessed and may not be exact ) The estimated cost was in the region of £3,000.','the annual/monthly cost This figure represents the annual cost of a loan.','labour/production/transport etc costs They had to pay £30,000 in legal costs.','running/operating costs (= the amount it costs to run a business, a machine etc ) The new technology is cheaper and the running costs are lower.','borrowing costs (= the amount it costs to borrow money from a bank ) Interest rates and borrowing costs are likely to be higher next year.','the cost of living (= the amount you need to pay for food, clothes etc ) People are complaining about the rising cost of living.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"His uncle’s a car dealer and let him buy the car at cost (= without making a profit ) .","translation":"عمویش فروشنده ماشین است و به او اجازه می دهد ماشین را به قیمت تمام شده (= بدون کسب سود) بخرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001111971.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
